namespace ArgentSea;
public sealed class UnexpectedSqlResultException : ApplicationException {
  UnexpectedSqlResultException();               // "The query results are missing an expected value."
  UnexpectedSqlResultException(string message);
  UnexpectedSqlResultException(string message, Exception innerException);
}
// Carries no properties beyond the message; the library always uses the message constructor with a message naming the query and the missing value.
// Raised when a query completed but its results lack something the caller's contract requires: (1) a requested output parameter of the three-value output read came back null/DBNull and the requested TValue for that value is a non-nullable value type (message "Database query {query} expected to output the value of {name}, but the database value was null.") -- when TValue can hold null (a reference type or Nullable<T>) the read returns null for that value instead of throwing; (2) Mapper.ModelFromReaderWithCollectionsHandler found fewer result sets than the model has collection-mapped properties (constructed by reflection inside the compiled handler, message naming the property and the expected result-set position).
// It is not a transient fault and is never retried by the resilience strategy: it indicates a mismatch between the query (procedure or statement) and the caller's expectations, so callers should treat it as a contract defect. A query whose output value may legitimately be null should request that value as a nullable type (e.g. int? or string).
